; cycle.pol — the smallest model whose derived category has a CYCLE: two
; situations, and a move each way.
;
; rules_base.pol's four situations form a DAG, and a DAG cannot distinguish a
; derivation graph that is acyclic by construction from one that merely has not
; been given the chance to loop. Here it has: `reach` derives every pair, so a
; fact recorded with any derivation other than its FIRST would name a premise
; that names it back.

(schema toggle
  (type flag (lo hi))
  (type box (arrow f (to flag))))

(instance i toggle
  (box b (f lo)))

(use toggle)
(initial i)

(transition up   (when (is b.f lo)) (do (set b.f hi)))
(transition down (when (is b.f hi)) (do (set b.f lo)))
